module

public import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.AdicSpace.Spa.StructurePresheaf.LaurentCover.Cech

import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.AdicSpace.Spa.Localization.Units
import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.AdicSpace.Spa.StructurePresheaf.LaurentCover.Sheaf

/-!
# The Čech complexes of standard rational covers

Let `A` be a strongly noetherian Tate ring, `A⁺` a subring of power-bounded elements, `W` a
rational subset of `X = Spa(A, A⁺)` and `T ⊆ A` a nonempty finite set. This file proves that the
standard rational cover of `W` generated by `T`, with pieces

```text
W ∩ R(T/t) = W ∩ {v | v(t') ≤ v(t) ≠ 0 for t' ∈ T},    t ∈ T,
```

is acyclic for the structure presheaf when the elements of `T` are units of `A`, more generally
when they vanish at no point of `W`, and finally whenever they generate the unit ideal: its
augmented Čech complex, as a presheaf of abelian groups on the opens contained in `W`, is exact in
every degree. These are Wedhorn's Lemma 8.34(iii) and (ii) in all degrees; the degree-zero
statements are `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.isSheafFor_ofArrows_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_isUnit`,
`TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.isSheafFor_ofArrows_inf_spaBasicOpen` and
`TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.isSheafFor_ofArrows_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_span_eq_top`.

The Laurent cover generated by the ratios `t t'⁻¹` refines the standard cover
(`laurentSieve_mul_inverse_le_ofArrows_inf_spaBasicOpen`). So on every rational subset `Y ⊆ W` on
which these ratios have fixed signs, the restriction of the standard cover to `Y` has `Y` itself as
a member, and is acyclic. Acyclicity then descends along the Laurent cover
(`quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_of_laurentSieve`).

In Wedhorn's proof of Lemma 8.34(ii), part (iii) is applied to standard covers of a rational
subset `W` generated by elements that vanish nowhere on `W`, rather than by units of `A`. Writing
`W = R(U/s)` and `B = A⟨U/s⟩`, such elements become units of `B`
(`isUnit_toCompletionLoc_iff_forall_notMem_supp`), the cover pulls back to the standard cover of
`Spa(B, A_U⁺)` generated by their images, `B` is again a strongly noetherian Tate ring, and
acyclicity passes between the two covers along Wedhorn's Remark 8.4
(`quasiIso_cechAugmentation_iff_locOpensComap`).

Let `T` be a finite set of generators and let `ϖ` be a unit such that at every point of
`Spa(A, A⁺)` some element of `T` strictly dominates `ϖ`. On a Laurent piece for the elements
`ϖ⁻¹ t`, the members of sign `≤` of the standard cover are empty. The members of sign `≥` can be
presented using only the generators of sign `≥`, which vanish nowhere on the Laurent piece.

This file proves that the two standard covers have the same Čech acyclicity when the generator
set of sign `≥` is nonempty. The covers refine one another, so Mathlib's formal coproduct Čech
homotopies, through `TauCeti.CategoryTheory.quasiIso_cechAugmentation_congr`, apply to every
presheaf with values in a preadditive category with homology and the required products. If
there are no generators of sign `≥`, the Laurent piece is empty and the original nonempty
cover has a member equal to the whole piece. Its augmentation is therefore a quasi-isomorphism
without any assumption on the value of the presheaf on the empty open.

The local reduction criterion is independent of the coordinate rings and requires neither
sheafiness nor noetherianness. For the structure presheaf over a strongly noetherian Tate ring,
Laurent-cover descent then reduces acyclicity of unit-ideal standard covers to acyclicity of
standard covers generated by elements vanishing nowhere on rational opens, which holds by the
previous step.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_isUnit`: over a
  strongly noetherian Tate ring, the standard rational cover of a rational subset generated by a
  nonempty finite set of units is acyclic for the structure presheaf.
* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen`: over a strongly
  noetherian Tate ring, the standard rational cover of a rational subset `W` generated by a
  nonempty finite set vanishing at no point of `W` is acyclic for the structure presheaf.
* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_span_eq_top_of_quasiIso`:
  acyclicity of unit-ideal standard covers reduces to acyclicity of standard covers generated by
  nowhere-vanishing elements on rational opens.
* `TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum.quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_span_eq_top`: over a
  strongly noetherian Tate ring, the standard rational cover of a rational subset generated by a
  nonempty finite set spanning the unit ideal is acyclic for the structure presheaf.

## References

* [T. Wedhorn, *Adic Spaces*][wedhorn_adic] (arXiv:1910.05934v1), Definition A.1, Remark 8.4 and
  Lemma 8.34(ii), (iii).
* S. Bosch, U. Güntzer, R. Remmert, *Non-Archimedean Analysis*, §8.2.2, Lemma 3, the
  rigid-analytic original.
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory Limits TopologicalSpace TauCeti.Huber TauCeti.Huber.PairOfDefinition
  TauCeti.CategoryTheory

universe v

namespace TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum

section Units

variable {A : Type v} [CommRing A] [UniformSpace A] [IsTopologicalRing A] [IsTateRing A]
  [IsStronglyNoetherian A] (P : PairOfDefinition A) {Aplus : Subring A}

/-- **Wedhorn's Lemma 8.34(iii): standard covers generated by units are acyclic.** Let `A` be a
strongly noetherian Tate ring, `A⁺` a subring of power-bounded elements, `W` a rational subset of
`Spa(A, A⁺)` and `T` a nonempty finite set of units of `A`. The augmented Čech complex of the
structure presheaf, as a presheaf of abelian groups on the opens contained in `W`, for the standard
rational cover `(W ∩ R(T/t))_{t ∈ T}` of `W` is exact in every degree. `A` itself need not be
complete. -/
theorem quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_isUnit
    (hAplus : ∀ ⦃a⦄, a ∈ Aplus → IsPowerBounded a) {T : Finset A} (hT : T.Nonempty)
    (hu : ∀ t ∈ T, IsUnit t) {W : Opens ↥(spa Aplus)} (hW : W ∈ spaRationalOpens Aplus) :
    QuasiIso (cechAugmentation
      (fun t : T ↦ (⟨W ⊓ spaBasicOpen Aplus T t, Set.mem_Iic.2 inf_le_left⟩ : Set.Iic W))
      isTerminalTop (presentationLimitAddCommGrpPresheaf P Aplus W)) := by
  classical
  -- `T` contains a unit, so it generates the unit ideal, which is open
  have hTopen : IsOpen (Ideal.span (T : Set A) : Set A) := by
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hT
    rw [Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ (Ideal.subset_span ht) (hu t ht)]
    exact isOpen_univ
  refine quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_of_laurentSieve P hAplus
    (Finset.univ.image fun p : T × T ↦ (p.1 : A) * Ring.inverse (p.2 : A)) hW
    (fun t : T ↦ spaBasicOpen Aplus T t) (fun _ ↦ spaBasicOpen_mem_spaRationalOpens hTopen)
    fun Y g _ hg ↦ ?_
  -- on a rational subset where the ratios `t t'⁻¹` have fixed signs, some piece contains `Y`
  obtain ⟨t, e, -⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff _ _ _).1
    (laurentSieve_mul_inverse_le_ofArrows_inf_spaBasicOpen hT hu W g hg)
  exact quasiIso_cechAugmentation_of_hom _ isTerminalTop _ (i₀ := t)
    (homOfLE (Subtype.mk_le_mk.2 (le_inf le_rfl (e.le.trans inf_le_right))))

/-- **Standard covers generated by elements vanishing nowhere are acyclic.** Let `A` be a strongly
noetherian Tate ring, `P` a pair of definition whose ring of definition lies in `A⁺`, `A⁺` a
subring of power-bounded elements, `W` a rational subset of `Spa(A, A⁺)` and `T` a nonempty finite
subset of `A` that vanishes at no point of `W`. The augmented Čech complex of the structure
presheaf, as a presheaf of abelian groups on the opens contained in `W`, for the standard rational
cover `(W ∩ R(T/t))_{t ∈ T}` of `W` is exact in every degree. The degree-zero statement is
`isSheafFor_ofArrows_inf_spaBasicOpen`.

The elements of `T` are units of the coordinate ring `B` of `W`, though not necessarily of `A`;
when they are units of `A`, see `quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_isUnit`, which
needs no hypothesis on `P`. -/
theorem quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen (hP : P.ringOfDefinition ≤ Aplus)
    (hAplus : ∀ ⦃a⦄, a ∈ Aplus → IsPowerBounded a) {T : Finset A} (hT : T.Nonempty)
    {W : Opens ↥(spa Aplus)} (hW : W ∈ spaRationalOpens Aplus)
    (hTW : ∀ t ∈ T, ∀ v ∈ W, t ∉ supp (v : Spv A)) :
    QuasiIso (cechAugmentation
      (fun t : T ↦ (⟨W ⊓ spaBasicOpen Aplus T t, Set.mem_Iic.2 inf_le_left⟩ : Set.Iic W))
      isTerminalTop (presentationLimitAddCommGrpPresheaf P Aplus W)) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨U, s, hU, hWU⟩ := mem_spaRationalFamily_iff.mp (mem_spaRationalOpens.mp hW)
  obtain rfl : W = spaBasicOpen Aplus U s :=
    Opens.ext (hWU.trans (Set.ext fun _ ↦ mem_spaBasicOpen.symm))
  -- `B = A⟨U/s⟩` is again a strongly noetherian Tate ring, with plus ring of power-bounded elements
  have hden := hasDenominatorPower_of_isOpen_span P U s (Localization.Away s) hU
  let _ := locUniformSpace P U s _ hden
  have _ := isUniformAddGroup_locUniformSpace P U s _ hden
  have _ := isTopologicalRing_locUniformSpace P U s _ hden
  have _ := isTateRing_completion_locTopology_of_isTateRing P U s _ hden
  have _ : IsStronglyNoetherian (UniformSpace.Completion (Localization.Away s)) :=
    laurentGluing_isStronglyNoetherian.completion_localization P U s hU
      (inferInstanceAs (IsStronglyNoetherian A))
  have hBplus := isPowerBounded_of_mem_completedPlusSubring P Aplus hAplus U s _ hden
  let ρ := toCompletionLoc P U s _ hden
  -- the elements of `T` vanish nowhere on `R(U/s)`, so they become units of `B`
  have hu : ∀ t' ∈ T.image ρ, IsUnit t' := by
    simp only [Finset.mem_image]
    rintro _ ⟨t, ht, rfl⟩
    exact (isUnit_toCompletionLoc_iff_forall_notMem_supp P Aplus hP hAplus U s _ hden t).2
      fun v hv ↦ hTW t ht ⟨v, rationalSubset_subset_spa Aplus U s hv⟩ (mem_spaBasicOpen.mpr hv)
  rw [quasiIso_cechAugmentation_iff_locOpensComap P U s _ hden hAplus hP hU le_rfl]
  -- the pieces pull back to the standard cover of `B` generated by the image of `T`
  have hpull (t : T) : locOpensComap P Aplus U s _ hden
      (spaBasicOpen Aplus U s ⊓ spaBasicOpen Aplus T t) =
        locOpensComap P Aplus U s _ hden (spaBasicOpen Aplus U s) ⊓
          spaBasicOpen (completedPlusSubring P Aplus U s _ hden) (T.image ρ) (ρ t) := by
    rw [locOpensComap_inf, locOpensComap_spaBasicOpen P Aplus U s _ hden T]
  -- reindex the standard cover of `B`, generated by the units `ρ t`, by `T`
  let W' := locOpensComap P Aplus U s _ hden (spaBasicOpen Aplus U s)
  let V (t : T) : Set.Iic W' := ⟨locOpensComap P Aplus U s _ hden
    (spaBasicOpen Aplus U s ⊓ spaBasicOpen Aplus T t),
      Set.mem_Iic.2 (locOpensComap_mono P Aplus U s _ hden inf_le_left)⟩
  let V' (t' : T.image ρ) : Set.Iic W' :=
    ⟨W' ⊓ spaBasicOpen (completedPlusSubring P Aplus U s _ hden) (T.image ρ) t',
      Set.mem_Iic.2 inf_le_left⟩
  have hsurj (t' : T.image ρ) : ∃ t : T, ρ t = t' := by
    obtain ⟨t, ht, e⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp t'.2
    exact ⟨⟨t, ht⟩, e⟩
  choose σ hσ using hsurj
  let φ : FormalCoproduct.mk _ V ⟶ FormalCoproduct.mk _ V' :=
    ⟨fun t ↦ ⟨ρ t, Finset.mem_image_of_mem ρ t.2⟩, fun t ↦ homOfLE (hpull t).le⟩
  let ψ : FormalCoproduct.mk _ V' ⟶ FormalCoproduct.mk _ V :=
    ⟨σ, fun t' ↦ homOfLE (by rw [Subtype.mk_le_mk, hpull, hσ])⟩
  exact (quasiIso_cechAugmentation_congr _ _ φ ψ).2
    (quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_isUnit (completionLocalization P U s _ hden)
      hBplus (hT.image ρ) hu (locOpensComap_mem_spaRationalOpens P Aplus U s _ hden hW))

end Units

section Topological

variable {A : Type v} [CommRing A] [TopologicalSpace A] {Aplus : Subring A}
  {D : Type*} [Category D] [Preadditive D] [HasProducts.{v} D] [HasZeroObject D]
  [CategoryWithHomology D] {T : Finset A} {ϖ : Aˣ} {J : Set T}
  {V : Opens ↥(spa Aplus)}

/-- **Čech invariance under the subcover of sign `≥` of a Laurent piece.** Suppose `T'` is
the nonempty finite set of generators of sign `≥`. On an open `V` contained in the Laurent
piece, suppose that at every point of `V` some element of `T` strictly dominates `ϖ`. Then the
standard covers generated by `T` and `T'` have quasi-isomorphic augmentations for exactly the
same presheaves. -/
theorem quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_iff_of_subset_laurentPiece
    (hϖ : ∀ v ∈ V, ∃ t ∈ T, v.1.toValuativeRel.vlt (ϖ : A) t)
    (hVJ : (V : Set ↥(spa Aplus)) ⊆
      Subtype.val ⁻¹' laurentPiece Aplus (fun t : T ↦ (ϖ⁻¹ : Aˣ) * (t : A)) J)
    {T' : Finset A} (hT' : T'.Nonempty)
    (hmem : ∀ a, a ∈ T' ↔ ∃ h : a ∈ T, (⟨a, h⟩ : T) ∈ J)
    (F : (Set.Iic V)ᵒᵖ ⥤ D) :
    QuasiIso (cechAugmentation
      (fun t : T ↦ (⟨V ⊓ spaBasicOpen Aplus T t, Set.mem_Iic.2 inf_le_left⟩ : Set.Iic V))
      isTerminalTop F) ↔
    QuasiIso (cechAugmentation
      (fun t : T' ↦ (⟨V ⊓ spaBasicOpen Aplus T' t, Set.mem_Iic.2 inf_le_left⟩ : Set.Iic V))
      isTerminalTop F) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨t₀, ht₀⟩ := hT'
  let f (t : T) : T' := if ht : t ∈ J then ⟨t, (hmem t).mpr ⟨t.2, ht⟩⟩ else ⟨t₀, ht₀⟩
  let g (t : T') : T := ⟨t, ((hmem t).mp t.2).1⟩
  refine quasiIso_cechAugmentation_congr _ _
    ⟨f, fun t ↦ homOfLE (Subtype.mk_le_mk.2 ?_)⟩
    ⟨g, fun t ↦ homOfLE (Subtype.mk_le_mk.2 ?_)⟩
  · by_cases ht : t ∈ J
    · simp only [f, dite_eq_left ht]
      exact (inf_spaBasicOpen_eq_inf_of_subset_laurentPiece hmem hVJ ht).le
    · simp only [f, dite_eq_right ht]
      rw [inf_spaBasicOpen_eq_bot_of_subset_laurentPiece hϖ hVJ ht]
      exact bot_le
  · have ht : g t ∈ J := ((hmem t).mp t.2).2
    exact (inf_spaBasicOpen_eq_inf_of_subset_laurentPiece hmem hVJ ht).symm.le

/-- **Reduction of Čech acyclicity on a Laurent piece to nowhere-vanishing generators.** If
standard covers generated by nonempty finite sets vanishing nowhere on `V` are acyclic for `F`,
and at every point of `V` some element of `T` strictly dominates `ϖ`, then the standard cover
generated by `T` is acyclic on `V`. The case of an empty generator set of sign `≥` needs no
additional hypothesis on `F`. -/
theorem quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_subset_laurentPiece_of_quasiIso
    (hT : T.Nonempty)
    (hϖ : ∀ v ∈ V, ∃ t ∈ T, v.1.toValuativeRel.vlt (ϖ : A) t)
    (hVJ : (V : Set ↥(spa Aplus)) ⊆
      Subtype.val ⁻¹' laurentPiece Aplus (fun t : T ↦ (ϖ⁻¹ : Aˣ) * (t : A)) J)
    (F : (Set.Iic V)ᵒᵖ ⥤ D)
    (hstandard : ∀ {T' : Finset A}, T'.Nonempty →
      (∀ t ∈ T', ∀ v ∈ V, t ∉ supp (v : Spv A)) →
      QuasiIso (cechAugmentation
        (fun t : T' ↦ (⟨V ⊓ spaBasicOpen Aplus T' t, Set.mem_Iic.2 inf_le_left⟩ : Set.Iic V))
        isTerminalTop F)) :
    QuasiIso (cechAugmentation
      (fun t : T ↦ (⟨V ⊓ spaBasicOpen Aplus T t, Set.mem_Iic.2 inf_le_left⟩ : Set.Iic V))
      isTerminalTop F) := by
  classical
  let T' := T.filter fun a ↦ ∃ h : a ∈ T, (⟨a, h⟩ : T) ∈ J
  have hmem (a : A) : a ∈ T' ↔ ∃ h : a ∈ T, (⟨a, h⟩ : T) ∈ J := by
    simp [T']
  rcases T'.eq_empty_or_nonempty with hT' | hT'
  · have hV : V = ⊥ := eq_bot_of_subset_laurentPiece_of_eq_empty hϖ
      (fun t ht ↦ (hmem t).mpr ⟨t.2, ht⟩) hVJ hT'
    obtain ⟨t₀, ht₀⟩ := hT
    exact quasiIso_cechAugmentation_of_hom _ isTerminalTop F (i₀ := ⟨t₀, ht₀⟩)
      (homOfLE (Subtype.mk_le_mk.2 (by simp [hV])))
  · exact (quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_iff_of_subset_laurentPiece
      hϖ hVJ hT' hmem F).2
      (hstandard hT' (notMem_supp_of_subset_laurentPiece (fun a ↦ (hmem a).mp) hVJ))

end Topological

section StronglyNoetherian

variable {A : Type v} [CommRing A] [UniformSpace A] [IsTopologicalRing A] [Huber.IsTateRing A]
  [Huber.IsStronglyNoetherian A] {Aplus : Subring A} {T : Finset A}

/-- **The unit-ideal standard-cover reduction in all degrees.** Over a strongly noetherian Tate
ring, acyclicity of standard covers generated by nowhere-vanishing elements on rational opens
implies acyclicity of standard covers generated by a finite set `T` spanning the unit ideal.
This is the reduction in Wedhorn's Lemma 8.34(ii). That input is
`quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen`, which gives
`quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_span_eq_top`. -/
theorem quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_span_eq_top_of_quasiIso
    (P : Huber.PairOfDefinition A)
    (hAplus : ∀ ⦃a⦄, a ∈ Aplus → Huber.IsPowerBounded a)
    (hT : T.Nonempty) (hspan : Ideal.span (T : Set A) = ⊤)
    {W : Opens ↥(spa Aplus)} (hW : W ∈ spaRationalOpens Aplus)
    (hstandard : ∀ {T' : Finset A}, T'.Nonempty → {Y : Opens ↥(spa Aplus)} →
      Y ∈ spaRationalOpens Aplus → (∀ t ∈ T', ∀ v ∈ Y, t ∉ supp (v : Spv A)) →
      QuasiIso (cechAugmentation
        (fun t : T' ↦ (⟨Y ⊓ spaBasicOpen Aplus T' t, Set.mem_Iic.2 inf_le_left⟩ : Set.Iic Y))
        isTerminalTop (presentationLimitAddCommGrpPresheaf P Aplus Y))) :
    QuasiIso (cechAugmentation
      (fun t : T ↦ (⟨W ⊓ spaBasicOpen Aplus T t, Set.mem_Iic.2 inf_le_left⟩ : Set.Iic W))
      isTerminalTop (presentationLimitAddCommGrpPresheaf P Aplus W)) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := exists_unit_forall_mem_spa_exists_vlt Aplus hspan
  have hTopen : IsOpen (Ideal.span (T : Set A) : Set A) := by
    rw [hspan]
    exact isOpen_univ
  let f : T → A := fun t ↦ (ϖ⁻¹ : Aˣ) * (t : A)
  refine quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_of_laurentSieve P hAplus (Finset.univ.image f) hW
    (fun t : T ↦ spaBasicOpen Aplus T t) (fun _ ↦ spaBasicOpen_mem_spaRationalOpens hTopen)
    fun Y g hY hg ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨J, hJ⟩ := (laurentSieve_image_apply_iff_exists_laurentPiece f g).mp hg
  exact quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_subset_laurentPiece_of_quasiIso
    hT (fun v _ ↦ hϖ v.1 v.2) hJ (presentationLimitAddCommGrpPresheaf P Aplus Y)
    fun hT' hvan ↦ hstandard hT' hY hvan

/-- **Wedhorn's Lemma 8.34(ii): standard covers generated by the unit ideal are acyclic.** Let `A`
be a strongly noetherian Tate ring, `P` a pair of definition whose ring of definition lies in `A⁺`,
`A⁺` a subring of power-bounded elements, `W` a rational subset of `Spa(A, A⁺)` and `T` a nonempty
finite subset of `A` generating the unit ideal. The augmented Čech complex of the structure
presheaf, as a presheaf of abelian groups on the opens contained in `W`, for the standard rational
cover `(W ∩ R(T/t))_{t ∈ T}` of `W` is exact in every degree. `A` itself need not be complete. The
degree-zero statement is `isSheafFor_ofArrows_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_span_eq_top`. -/
theorem quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_span_eq_top
    (P : Huber.PairOfDefinition A) (hP : P.ringOfDefinition ≤ Aplus)
    (hAplus : ∀ ⦃a⦄, a ∈ Aplus → Huber.IsPowerBounded a)
    (hT : T.Nonempty) (hspan : Ideal.span (T : Set A) = ⊤)
    {W : Opens ↥(spa Aplus)} (hW : W ∈ spaRationalOpens Aplus) :
    QuasiIso (cechAugmentation
      (fun t : T ↦ (⟨W ⊓ spaBasicOpen Aplus T t, Set.mem_Iic.2 inf_le_left⟩ : Set.Iic W))
      isTerminalTop (presentationLimitAddCommGrpPresheaf P Aplus W)) :=
  quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen_of_span_eq_top_of_quasiIso P hAplus hT hspan hW
    fun {_} hT' {_} hY hvan ↦ quasiIso_cechAugmentation_inf_spaBasicOpen P hP hAplus hT' hY hvan

end StronglyNoetherian

end TauCeti.ValuationSpectrum
